IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 5 Division 3, ss 188 and 189 -- minutes of proceedings and inspection of minute books.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). "Within one month of the date" is counted by the keel's P1 and P4 (the day of the meeting is not counted; a month ends on the corresponding date).
-- "Within a reasonable time" (188(3B), (3C)) is no number of days: it is an input the person states (F-40).

§ `Section 188(1): the duty to enter and sign minutes`

-- (1)(a): "Every company must cause -- (a) minutes of all proceedings of general meetings and of meetings of its directors and of its chief executive officers (if any) to be entered in books kept for that purpose within one month
-- of the date upon which the relevant meeting was held".
-- src:16998 | 188.—(1) Every company must cause —
-- src:17000 | (a) minutes of all proceedings of general meetings and of
-- src:17001 | meetings of its directors and of its chief executive officers
-- src:17002 | (if any) to be entered in books kept for that purpose within
-- src:17003 | one month of the date upon which the relevant meeting was
-- src:17004 | held; and
@ref s 188(1)(a) (src:16998-17004)
GIVEN `the proceedings are those of a general meeting, or of a meeting of its directors or of its chief executive officers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date upon which the relevant meeting was held` IS A DATE
      `the date the minutes were entered in a book kept for that purpose` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(1)(a) the company has caused the minutes to be entered in a book within one month` MEANS
    IF NOT `the proceedings are those of a general meeting, or of a meeting of its directors or of its chief executive officers`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "minutes of all proceedings of general meetings and of meetings of its directors and of its chief executive officers (if any)" (a duty's own question; the proceedings are not of those meetings)
    ELSE (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date upon which the relevant meeting was held` `the date the minutes were entered in a book kept for that purpose` 1 Months
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "to be entered in books kept for that purpose within one month of the date upon which the relevant meeting was held" (a duty's own question; a period the text fixes)

GIVEN `the date upon which the relevant meeting was held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 188(1)(a) the number of days from the meeting to the last day for entering the minutes` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date upon which the relevant meeting was held` 1 Months) MINUS `the date upon which the relevant meeting was held`

-- (1)(b): "those minutes to be signed by the chairperson of the meeting at which the proceedings were had or by the chairperson of the next succeeding meeting." No time limit and no number is stated.
-- src:17006 | (b) those minutes to be signed by the chairperson of the
-- src:17007 | meeting at which the proceedings were had or by the
-- src:17008 | chairperson of the next succeeding meeting.
@ref s 188(1)(b) (src:17006-17008)
GIVEN `the minutes are signed by the chairperson of the meeting at which the proceedings were had` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minutes are signed by the chairperson of the next succeeding meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(1)(b) the minutes have been signed by the chairperson of the meeting or of the next succeeding meeting` MEANS
    IF `the minutes are signed by the chairperson of the meeting at which the proceedings were had` OR `the minutes are signed by the chairperson of the next succeeding meeting`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "those minutes to be signed by the chairperson of the meeting at which the proceedings were had or by the chairperson of the next succeeding meeting" (a duty's own question)

§ `Section 188(2) and (3): minutes as evidence`

-- (2): "Any minutes so entered that purport to be signed as provided in subsection (1) are evidence of the proceedings to which they relate, unless the contrary is proved." An "unless" once met: decided case by case (F-45).
-- src:17012 | (2) Any minutes so entered that purport to be signed as provided in
-- src:17013 | subsection (1) are evidence of the proceedings to which they relate,
-- src:17014 | unless the contrary is proved.
@ref s 188(2) (src:17012-17014)
GIVEN `the minutes are entered in a book and purport to be signed as provided in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(2) the minutes are evidence of the proceedings to which they relate` MEANS
    IF NOT `the minutes are entered in a book and purport to be signed as provided in subsection (1)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "minutes so entered that purport to be signed as provided in subsection (1)"
    ELSE (IF `the contrary is proved`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are evidence of the proceedings to which they relate, unless the contrary is proved" -- the contrary is proved, so this subsection gives no evidence on these facts (an "unless" once met; F-45)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- (3): "Where minutes have been so entered and signed, then, until the contrary is proved -- (a) the meeting is deemed to have been duly held and convened; (b) all proceedings had thereat are deemed to have been duly had; and
-- (c) all appointments of officers or liquidators made thereat are deemed to be valid." A "where" gate on a deeming is JUST FALSE when it fails (periods ruling (b)); "until the contrary is proved" ends the deeming (ruling (d), the "until" bar).
-- src:17016 | (3) Where minutes have been so entered and signed, then, until the
-- src:17017 | contrary is proved —
-- src:17019 | (a) the meeting is deemed to have been duly held and
-- src:17020 | convened;
-- src:17022 | (b) all proceedings had thereat are deemed to have been duly
-- src:17023 | had; and
-- src:17025 | (c) all appointments of officers or liquidators made thereat are
-- src:17026 | deemed to be valid.
@ref s 188(3) (src:17016-17026)
GIVEN `the minutes have been entered and signed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(3)(a) the meeting is deemed to have been duly held and convened` MEANS
    IF `the minutes have been entered and signed` AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where minutes have been so entered and signed, then, until the contrary is proved -- (a) the meeting is deemed to have been duly held and convened" (a "where" gate on a deeming; an "until" bar)

@ref s 188(3) (src:17016-17026)
GIVEN `the minutes have been entered and signed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(3)(b) all proceedings had at the meeting are deemed to have been duly had` MEANS
    IF `the minutes have been entered and signed` AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where minutes have been so entered and signed, then, until the contrary is proved -- (b) all proceedings had thereat are deemed to have been duly had" (a "where" gate on a deeming; an "until" bar)

@ref s 188(3) (src:17016-17026)
GIVEN `the minutes have been entered and signed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment of an officer or liquidator was made at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(3)(c) the appointment of the officer or liquidator is deemed to be valid` MEANS
    IF `the minutes have been entered and signed` AND `the appointment of an officer or liquidator was made at the meeting` AND (NOT `the contrary is proved`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where minutes have been so entered and signed, then, until the contrary is proved -- (c) all appointments of officers or liquidators made thereat are deemed to be valid" (a "where" gate on a deeming; an "until" bar)

§ `Section 188(3A) to (3D): the minute books of sole directors and written resolutions`

DECLARE `s 188(3A) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 188(3A)(a)(i) a resolution passed by the sole director`
    `s 188(3A)(a)(ii) a declaration made by the sole director`
    `s 188(3A)(b) a resolution passed by written means under section 184A`

-- (3A): "Every company must keep minute books in which it must cause to be entered the following matters: (a) if the company has only one director -- (i) the passing of resolutions by that director; and (ii) the making of declarations by that
-- director; (b) resolutions passed by written means under section 184A, within one month of the passing or making of each resolution or declaration."
-- src:17028 | (3A) Every company must keep minute books in which it must
-- src:17029 | cause to be entered the following matters:
-- src:17031 | (a) if the company has only one director —
-- src:17033 | (i) the passing of resolutions by that director; and
-- src:17035 | (ii) the making of declarations by that director;
-- src:17037 | (b) resolutions passed by written means under section 184A,
-- src:17039 | within one month of the passing or making of each resolution or
-- src:17040 | declaration.
@ref s 188(3A) (src:17028-17040)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 188(3A) matter`
      `the company has only one director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 188(3A) the duty to enter the matter applies` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 188(3A)(a)(i) a resolution passed by the sole director` THEN `the company has only one director`
    WHEN `s 188(3A)(a)(ii) a declaration made by the sole director` THEN `the company has only one director`
    WHEN `s 188(3A)(b) a resolution passed by written means under section 184A` THEN TRUE

@ref s 188(3A) (src:17028-17040)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 188(3A) matter`
      `the company has only one director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the resolution was passed or the declaration was made` IS A DATE
      `the day the matter was entered in the minute book` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(3A) the company has entered the matter in a minute book within one month` MEANS
    IF NOT `s 188(3A) the duty to enter the matter applies` matter `the company has only one director`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) if the company has only one director -- (i) the passing of resolutions by that director; and (ii) the making of declarations by that director" (an "if" gate on a duty: the duty does not arise on these facts)
    ELSE (IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the resolution was passed or the declaration was made` `the day the matter was entered in the minute book` 1 Months
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within one month of the passing or making of each resolution or declaration" (a duty's own question; a period the text fixes)

GIVEN `the day the resolution was passed or the declaration was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 188(3A) the number of days from the passing or making to the last day for entering the matter` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the resolution was passed or the declaration was made` 1 Months) MINUS `the day the resolution was passed or the declaration was made`

-- src:17045 | (3B) The company must ensure that minutes of the passing of a
-- src:17046 | resolution mentioned in subsection (3A)(b) are signed by a director
-- src:17047 | within a reasonable time after the resolution is passed.
@ref s 188(3B) (src:17045-17047)
GIVEN `the minutes are of the passing of a resolution mentioned in subsection (3A)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minutes are signed by a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they were signed within a reasonable time after the resolution was passed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(3B) the company has ensured that the minutes are signed by a director within a reasonable time` MEANS
    IF `the minutes are of the passing of a resolution mentioned in subsection (3A)(b)` AND `the minutes are signed by a director` AND `they were signed within a reasonable time after the resolution was passed`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The company must ensure that minutes of the passing of a resolution mentioned in subsection (3A)(b) are signed by a director within a reasonable time after the resolution is passed" (a duty's own question; "within a reasonable time" read as an input, F-40)

-- src:17049 | (3C) The director of a company with only one director who has
-- src:17050 | passed a resolution or made a declaration must sign the minutes
-- src:17051 | thereof within a reasonable time after the resolution is passed or the
-- src:17052 | declaration is made.
@ref s 188(3C) (src:17049-17052)
GIVEN `the company has only one director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that director has passed a resolution or made a declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has signed the minutes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director signed them within a reasonable time after the resolution was passed or the declaration made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(3C) the sole director has signed the minutes within a reasonable time` MEANS
    IF `the company has only one director` AND `that director has passed a resolution or made a declaration` AND `the director has signed the minutes` AND `the director signed them within a reasonable time after the resolution was passed or the declaration made`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The director of a company with only one director who has passed a resolution or made a declaration must sign the minutes thereof within a reasonable time" (a duty's own question; "within a reasonable time" read as an input, F-40)

-- src:17054 | (3D) Minutes entered in accordance with subsection (3A) and
-- src:17055 | purportedly signed in accordance with subsection (3B) or (3C) (as the
-- src:17056 | case may be) are evidence of the resolution or declaration to which
-- src:17057 | they relate, unless the contrary is proved.
@ref s 188(3D) (src:17054-17057)
GIVEN `the minutes are entered in accordance with subsection (3A) and purportedly signed in accordance with subsection (3B) or (3C)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(3D) the minutes are evidence of the resolution or declaration to which they relate` MEANS
    IF NOT `the minutes are entered in accordance with subsection (3A) and purportedly signed in accordance with subsection (3B) or (3C)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "minutes entered in accordance with subsection (3A) and purportedly signed in accordance with subsection (3B) or (3C)"
    ELSE (IF `the contrary is proved`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "are evidence of the resolution or declaration to which they relate, unless the contrary is proved" -- the contrary is proved, so this subsection gives no evidence on these facts (an "unless" once met; F-45)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

§ `Section 188(4): the offence`

-- src:17059 | (4) If default is made in complying with this section, the company
-- src:17060 | and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of
-- src:17061 | an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:17062 | $2,000 and also to a default penalty.
@ref s 188(4) (src:17059-17062)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 188` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 188(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `default is made in complying with section 188` AND `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), F-10): "If default is made in complying with this section, the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

@ref s 188(4) (src:17059-17062)
GIVEN `default is made in complying with section 188` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 188(4) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 188(4) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `default is made in complying with section 188` `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 2000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $2,000, and also a default penalty; no imprisonment
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Section 189: inspection of minute books`

-- (2A): "Subsection (1) does not apply to books containing minutes of proceedings of meetings of a company's directors and of its chief executive officers, or (as the case may be) books containing minutes of the passing of resolutions
-- and the making of declarations by the director of a company that has only one director; and subsection (2) does not apply to any of those minutes." A flat negative (N2).
-- src:17076 | (2A) Subsection (1) does not apply to books containing minutes of
-- src:17077 | proceedings of meetings of a company’s directors and of its chief
-- src:17078 | executive officers, or (as the case may be) books containing minutes
-- src:17079 | of the passing of resolutions and the making of declarations by the
-- src:17080 | director of a company that has only one director; and subsection (2)
-- src:17081 | does not apply to any of those minutes.
@ref s 189(2A) (src:17076-17081)
GIVEN `the book contains minutes of proceedings of meetings of the company's directors or of its chief executive officers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the book contains minutes of the passing of resolutions and the making of declarations by the director of a company that has only one director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 189(2A) the book is one to which subsections (1) and (2) do not apply` MEANS
    IF `the book contains minutes of proceedings of meetings of the company's directors or of its chief executive officers` OR `the book contains minutes of the passing of resolutions and the making of declarations by the director of a company that has only one director`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of those books

-- (1): "The books mentioned in section 188(1) and (3A) must be kept by the company at the registered office or the principal place of business in Singapore of the company, and must be open to the inspection of any member without charge."
-- src:17066 | 189.—(1) The books mentioned in section 188(1) and (3A) must be
-- src:17067 | kept by the company at the registered office or the principal place of
-- src:17068 | business in Singapore of the company, and must be open to the
-- src:17069 | inspection of any member without charge.
@ref s 189(1) (src:17066-17069)
GIVEN `the book is one mentioned in section 188(1) or (3A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (2A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 189(1) the company must keep the book at the registered office or the principal place of business in Singapore` MEANS
    IF NOT `the book is one mentioned in section 188(1) or (3A)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "the books mentioned in section 188(1) and (3A)"
    ELSE (IF `the answer under subsection (2A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to books containing minutes of proceedings of meetings of a company's directors and of its chief executive officers" (a flat negative; N2)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

@ref s 189(1) (src:17066-17069)
GIVEN `the book is one mentioned in section 188(1) or (3A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (2A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 189(1) the book must be open to the inspection of the member without charge` MEANS
    IF NOT `the book is one mentioned in section 188(1) or (3A)`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks of "the books mentioned in section 188(1) and (3A)"
    ELSE (IF `the answer under subsection (2A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not apply to books containing minutes of proceedings of meetings of a company's directors and of its chief executive officers" (a flat negative; N2)
          ELSE (IF `the person is a member of the company`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING))   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection gives the inspection to "any member"

-- (2): "Any member is entitled to be furnished within 14 days after the member has made a request in writing in that behalf to the company with a copy of any minutes specified in section 188(1) or (3A) at a charge not exceeding $1 for every page thereof."
-- An "entitled"-named function: the general rule (an "if" or "where" gate that fails is JUST FALSE), listed in the fork register (F-28).
-- src:17071 | (2) Any member is entitled to be furnished within 14 days after the
-- src:17072 | member has made a request in writing in that behalf to the company
-- src:17073 | with a copy of any minutes specified in section 188(1) or (3A) at a
-- src:17074 | charge not exceeding $1 for every page thereof.
@ref s 189(2) (src:17071-17074)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member has made a request in writing in that behalf to the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the minutes are specified in section 188(1) or (3A)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer under subsection (2A)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 189(2) the member is entitled to be furnished with a copy of the minutes` MEANS
    IF NOT `the person is a member of the company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection gives the entitlement to "any member"
    ELSE (IF `the answer under subsection (2A)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "subsection (2) does not apply to any of those minutes" (a flat negative; N2)
          ELSE (IF `the member has made a request in writing in that behalf to the company` AND `the minutes are specified in section 188(1) or (3A)`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is entitled to be furnished ... after the member has made a request in writing ... with a copy of any minutes specified in section 188(1) or (3A)" (an entitled-named function; the general rule, F-28)

@ref s 189(2) (src:17071-17074)
GIVEN `the date the member made the request in writing` IS A DATE
      `the date the company furnished the copy` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 189(2) the copy was furnished within 14 days after the request` MEANS
    `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date the member made the request in writing` `the date the company furnished the copy` 14 Days

GIVEN `the date the member made the request in writing` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 189(2) the number of days from the request to the last day for furnishing the copy` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the member made the request in writing` 14 Days) MINUS `the date the member made the request in writing`

@ref s 189(2) (src:17071-17074)
GIVEN `the number of pages of the minutes` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 189(2) the most the company may charge for the copy` MEANS
    `the number of pages of the minutes`

-- src:17085 | (3) If any copy required under this section is not so furnished the
-- src:17086 | company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be
-- src:17087 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
