`s 189(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` MEANS
    IF `a copy required under section 189 is not furnished` AND `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the subsection's own question; split site (i), F-10): "If any copy required under this section is not so furnished the company and every officer of the company who is in default shall be guilty of an offence" -- an element is unmet

@ref s 189(3) (src:17085-17088)
GIVEN `a copy required under section 189 is not furnished` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 189(3) the most the person may be sentenced to on conviction` MEANS
    IF `s 189(3) the person is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` `a copy required under section 189 is not furnished` `the person is the company or an officer of the company who is in default` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST (Penalty OF 400, 0, FALSE, TRUE)   -- a fine not exceeding $400, and also a default penalty; no imprisonment
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection states a penalty only for the person it makes guilty

§ `Regulative rules of ss 188 and 189`

DECLARE `s 188 and s 189 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 188(1)(a) enter the minutes in a book`
    `s 188(1)(b) have the minutes signed by the chairperson`
    `s 188(3A) enter the matter in a minute book`
    `s 188(3B) ensure the minutes are signed by a director`
    `s 188(3C) sign the minutes`
    `s 189(1) keep the books at the registered office or the principal place of business in Singapore`
    `s 189(2) furnish a copy of the minutes`

-- s 188(1)(a): time 0 is the day of the meeting; the last day is one month later.
-- src:16998 | 188.—(1) Every company must cause —
-- src:17000 | (a) minutes of all proceedings of general meetings and of
-- src:17001 | meetings of its directors and of its chief executive officers
-- src:17002 | (if any) to be entered in books kept for that purpose within
-- src:17003 | one month of the date upon which the relevant meeting was
-- src:17004 | held; and
@ref s 188(1)(a) (src:16998-17004)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the date upon which the relevant meeting was held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 188 and s 189 act`
`s 188(1)(a) the company must cause the minutes to be entered in a book within one month` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 188(1)(a) enter the minutes in a book`
    WITHIN (`s 188(1)(a) the number of days from the meeting to the last day for entering the minutes` `the date upon which the relevant meeting was held`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not cause the minutes to be entered in a book within one month of the date upon which the relevant meeting was held"

-- s 188(1)(b): no time limit and no consequence is stated.
-- src:17006 | (b) those minutes to be signed by the chairperson of the
-- src:17007 | meeting at which the proceedings were had or by the
-- src:17008 | chairperson of the next succeeding meeting.
@ref s 188(1)(b) (src:17006-17008)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 188 and s 189 act`
`s 188(1)(b) the company must cause the minutes to be signed by the chairperson (no time limit)` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 188(1)(b) have the minutes signed by the chairperson`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 188(1)(b) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not cause the minutes to be signed by the chairperson of the meeting or of the next succeeding meeting" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: other; see notes]

-- s 188(3A): time 0 is the day the resolution was passed or the declaration made; the last day is one month later.
-- src:17028 | (3A) Every company must keep minute books in which it must
-- src:17029 | cause to be entered the following matters:
-- src:17031 | (a) if the company has only one director —
-- src:17033 | (i) the passing of resolutions by that director; and
-- src:17035 | (ii) the making of declarations by that director;
-- src:17037 | (b) resolutions passed by written means under section 184A,
-- src:17039 | within one month of the passing or making of each resolution or
-- src:17040 | declaration.
@ref s 188(3A) (src:17028-17040)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the day the resolution was passed or the declaration was made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 188 and s 189 act`
`s 188(3A) the company must cause the matter to be entered in a minute book within one month` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 188(3A) enter the matter in a minute book`
    WITHIN (`s 188(3A) the number of days from the passing or making to the last day for entering the matter` `the day the resolution was passed or the declaration was made`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not cause the matter to be entered in a minute book within one month of the passing or making of the resolution or declaration"

-- s 188(3B) and (3C): "within a reasonable time" is no number of days: the section's own standard of time is the input `the period the standard of time allows, as found` (s 52 does not apply, the section prescribes its own standard).
-- src:17045 | (3B) The company must ensure that minutes of the passing of a
-- src:17046 | resolution mentioned in subsection (3A)(b) are signed by a director
-- src:17047 | within a reasonable time after the resolution is passed.
@ref s 188(3B) (src:17045-17047)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("within a reasonable time") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 188 and s 189 act`
`s 188(3B) the company must ensure that the minutes are signed by a director` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 188(3B) ensure the minutes are signed by a director`
    WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section says "within a reasonable time", its own standard of time, found as an input; Interpretation Act 1965 s 52 does not apply, because the section prescribes its own standard (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not ensure that the minutes were signed by a director within a reasonable time"

-- src:17049 | (3C) The director of a company with only one director who has
-- src:17050 | passed a resolution or made a declaration must sign the minutes
-- src:17051 | thereof within a reasonable time after the resolution is passed or the
-- src:17052 | declaration is made.
@ref s 188(3C) (src:17049-17052)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the period the standard of time allows, as found` IS A NUMBER @desc The days that the standard of time in the section ("within a reasonable time") allows for this duty, found by whoever applies the rule; there is no default
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 188 and s 189 act`
`s 188(3C) the sole director must sign the minutes` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 188(3C) sign the minutes`
    WITHIN `the period the standard of time allows, as found`   -- the section says "within a reasonable time", its own standard of time, found as an input; Interpretation Act 1965 s 52 does not apply, because the section prescribes its own standard (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the director did not sign the minutes within a reasonable time"

-- s 189(1): a standing duty of the company with no period and no consequence stated in the subsection: no WITHIN, so no trace can reach BREACH (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
-- src:17066 | 189.—(1) The books mentioned in section 188(1) and (3A) must be
-- src:17067 | kept by the company at the registered office or the principal place of
-- src:17068 | business in Singapore of the company, and must be open to the
-- src:17069 | inspection of any member without charge.
@ref s 189(1) (src:17066-17069)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 188 and s 189 act`
`s 189(1) the company must keep the books at the registered office or the principal place of business in Singapore (no time limit)` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 189(1) keep the books at the registered office or the principal place of business in Singapore`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 189(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not keep the books at the registered office or the principal place of business in Singapore" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md) [class: maintenance; see notes]

-- s 189(2): time 0 is the day the member makes the request in writing; the last day is 14 days later.
-- src:17071 | (2) Any member is entitled to be furnished within 14 days after the
-- src:17072 | member has made a request in writing in that behalf to the company
-- src:17073 | with a copy of any minutes specified in section 188(1) or (3A) at a
-- src:17074 | charge not exceeding $1 for every page thereof.
@ref s 189(2) (src:17071-17074)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 188 and s 189 act`
`s 189(2) the company must furnish the member with a copy of the minutes within 14 days` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 189(2) furnish a copy of the minutes`
    WITHIN 14
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not furnish the member with a copy of the minutes within 14 days after the member made the request in writing"
